    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 **264 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI converted owner deletion to a soft-delete. Changes made:\n\n**`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `deleted` boolean field (`@Column(name = \"deleted\", nullable = false)`) with `isDeleted()`/`setDeleted()`. As a primitive it defaults to `false`, so a newly created owner is not deleted.\n\n**`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**\n- `deleteOwner(...)` now sets `owner.setDeleted(true)` and calls `saveOwner` instead of removing the row, still returning `204 No Content` (2xx). The row is retained, so `GET /api/owners/{id}` continues to return the owner with `deleted: true`.\n- The two blocking create checks \u2014 household occupancy and identity-key duplicate \u2014 now `continue` past any owner flagged deleted, so a normally-blocking duplicate is allowed when the only match has been soft-deleted.\n\n**`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `deleted` boolean property to the `Owner` schema. This regenerates `OwnerDto.getDeleted()`, and MapStruct auto-wires `owner.isDeleted() \u2192 ownerDto.setDeleted(...)` (verified in the generated `OwnerMapperImpl`).\n\n**DB schemas** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added a `deleted` column defaulting to false / NOT NULL so existing seed rows read back as not deleted.\n\nThe two new acceptance tests (`coreSoftDeleteFlagsAndRetains`, `coreDeletedOwnerIgnoredByDuplicateCheck`) pass, the existing `deleteOwnerSuccess` (expects 204) and `deleteOwnerNotFound` (expects 404) still pass, and the whole suite remains green.",
